      "text": "To find the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) for which \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\) factors into a product of two binomials with integer coefficients, we need to express \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\) in the form \\( (x + p)(x + q) \\).\n\nLet's expand \\( (x + p)(x + q) \\):\n\\[\n(x + p)(x + q) = x^2 + (p+q)x + pq\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n\\[\npq = 2008\n\\]\n\nWe need to find pairs of integers \\( (p, q) \\) such that their product is 2008. Each pair will contribute to the coefficient \\( b \\) of the linear term \\( bx \\). Specifically:\n\n\\[\nb = p + q\n\\]\n\nTo minimize \\( b \\), we need to choose \\( p \\) and \\( q \\) such that their sum \\( p + q \\) is minimized. We will start by examining possible factor pairs of 2008.\n\nFirst, we factorize 2008 to identify its factors:\n\\[\n2008 = 2^3 \\times 251\n\\]\n\nNext, we list all pairs \\((p, q)\\) such that \\( pq = 2008 \\):\n\\[\n(1, 2008), (2, 1004), (4, 502), (8, 251), (-1, -2008), (-2, -1004), (-4, -502), (-8, -251)\n\\]\n\nCalculating the pairs pairs:\n\\[\n1 + 2008 = 2009\n\\]\n\\[\n2 + 1004 = 1006\n\\]\n\\[\n4 + 502 = 506\n\\]\n\\[\n8 + 251 = 259\n\\]\n\\[\n-1 - 2008 = -2009\n\\]\n\\[\n-2 - 1004 = -1006\n\\]\n\\[\n-4 - 502 = -506\n\\]\n\\[\n-8 - 251 = -259\n\\]\n\nAmong all pairs, the smallest value of \\( p + q \\) is 259. This occurs when \\( p = 8 \\) and \\( q = 251 \\).\n\nThus, the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) is:\n\\[\nb = 8 + 251 = 259\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{259}\n\\]",
